From d789d6db492fd12b1ec1abb3f699fff5dd662287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:58:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Binary-length bounds: one home each; the inline transports
 cite it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

two_pow_bits_le (2^|bits L| ≤ 2L for L ≥ 1) moves from Codec/Layout to Machines/Bin, beside
length_bits_le; Codec/Parse, Logspace/PathHard, Randomized/RandomWalkPad, Randomized/BPLInP and
Randomized/SpaceAmplifyPoly's two_pow_bits_le now cite it. Codec/Word publishes wP_eq, and
Codec/Layout's wP_le cites Turing.length_bits_le_self through it; TQBFHardParams' restatement
of Codec.wP_le is removed. PrimeFind, CodeSimulator, RecordTable and SpaceAmplifyPoly's ell_le
cite length_bits_le_self; ISCountGenCorrect's bits_succ_le cites length_bits_le, PathHard's
ell_mono length_bits_mono, and WindowClock record_pos_lt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
